---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
import PhotoHero from "@dst/ui/district/PhotoHero.astro";
import { siteHeaderImage, currentUnits } from "../content";
---
<Layout
  title="Golden Visa Eligibility"
  description="Every Palm Central unit type clears the AED 2 million Golden Visa threshold. What that gets you, and how the property route actually works."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <PhotoHero
      eyebrow="Golden Visa"
      title="Every unit here clears the threshold"
      image={siteHeaderImage.src}
      imageAlt={siteHeaderImage.alt}
    />
    <p class="lede">
      Properties valued at <strong>AED 2 million</strong> and above generally
      qualify for UAE Golden Visa sponsorship. The cheapest unit currently
      for sale at Palm Central — a <strong>1-bedroom apartment from
      AED 2.7M</strong> — already clears it by a margin, and every larger
      unit type clears it further.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Where each unit type sits against the threshold</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Unit type</th><th>From (AED)</th><th>Above the AED 2M threshold by</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {currentUnits.map((u) => {
            const val = parseFloat(u.priceFrom.replace(/[^0-9.]/g, ""));
            const over = (val - 2).toFixed(1);
            return <tr><td>{u.type}</td><td>{u.priceFrom}</td><td>+AED {over}M</td></tr>;
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="note">
    Thresholds and eligibility criteria are set by UAE federal authorities
    and can change. This page tells you where Palm Central's pricing sits
    relative to the AED 2M mark — confirm current requirements before
    treating any purchase as a guaranteed Golden Visa route.
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What the Golden Visa route actually involves</h2>
    <p>
      Buying above the threshold is the entry condition, not the whole
      process — there's still an application, standard medical and
      Emirates ID formalities, and ownership conditions that can affect
      <strong>off-plan purchases</strong> specifically (mortgaged value and
      off-plan status are sometimes treated differently from a completed,
      unmortgaged property). We cover the mechanics in more depth on the
      network's
      dedicated visa site, including what an off-plan purchase like this
      one does and doesn't guarantee: see
      <a href="https://visas.dst.llc/golden/" title="Golden Visa via property investment — visas.dst.llc">Golden Visa via property investment</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you're weighing this against a completed-property route instead
      of off-plan, <a href="https://visas.dst.llc/properties/" title="Properties eligible for the Golden Visa — visas.dst.llc">eligible properties</a> covers
      what currently qualifies more broadly, and
      <a href="https://visas.dst.llc/family/" title="Family and lifestyle under the Golden Visa — visas.dst.llc">family and lifestyle</a> covers
      what a Golden Visa changes day to day once you have it — schooling,
      healthcare, and sponsorship for dependents.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container cta">
    <h2>Next step</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/#interest" title="Register interest in Palm Central">Register your interest</a> in
      a specific unit, or start with the
      <a href="https://visas.dst.llc/consultation/" title="Request a Golden Visa consultation — visas.dst.llc">Golden Visa consultation</a> if
      residency is the primary driver rather than the property itself.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .cta { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
